{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<pre><code>forms := form.NewTranslatedForm(func(loc form.Localizer, key string, args ...any) string {
    return tr.Tl(loc, key, args...)
})
forms.SetTheme("plain")
errs := forms.ValidateFormLocalized(&amp;input, loc)</code></pre>
<p>Here <code>tr</code> is a loaded go-translator instance and <code>loc</code> implements <code>GetLocale() string</code>. Load the PO languages before configuring the renderer; do not set a global current locale during a request.</p>
<pre><code>{{"{{"}} form_render_localized .Loc .Form .Errors }}</code></pre>
<h2>Catalogue keys</h2>
<pre><code>msgid "Name"
msgstr "Naam"

msgid "Save contact"
msgstr "Contact opslaan"

msgid "form||Validation required"
msgstr "Dit veld is verplicht."

msgid "form||Value should not exceed %d characters"
msgstr "Gebruik maximaal %d tekens."</code></pre>
<p>The callback receives labels, placeholders, descriptions, submit/cancel text and built-in validation keys. Keep the exact built-in key and preserve its formatting placeholders. The required marker in the standard label has a separate <a href="{{ basePath }}/themes" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/themes" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">theme customization</a> option.</p>
<h2>Choices and custom messages</h2>
<p>Use <code>translate:"true"</code> when enum values should pass through the translation callback. Custom validation messages and <code>errorMsg</code> values need an explicit application translation policy; they are not automatically converted into domain error codes.</p>
<p>Template key extraction does not scan struct tags or Go validation keys. Add those keys to the catalogue through your preparation/editing workflow or runtime discovery. Use the same localizer for validation and redisplay so a request does not mix languages.</p>
</article>
